# The bytes in this repository are the bytes of the release.
#
# `npm pack` hashes file contents, and the release is pinned by that hash. With
# git's line-ending conversion left to the client, a clone on a machine where
# `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows default, and the setting on the machine this
# was packed from — would check out CRLF where the repository stores LF, and
# every text file in the package would differ. The published SHA-256 would then
# be unreproducible from its own source, which is the one thing a pinned hash is
# for.
#
# `-text` means: never convert, in either direction. What was committed is what
# is checked out, on every platform.
* -text
